or `??=`assignsavalueifitis `null`.¶¶Boxing:¶-Ifyouboxa `Nullable`variablewith `null`itreturns `null`insteadofboxing.¶-Ifthevariablehasavalue ,itisboxedasusual.¶¶Unboxing:¶-Aboxedvaluetype `T`canbeunboxedto `T`orto `Nullable<T>`.¶-Iftheboxedvalueis `null`,unboxingto `Nullable<T>`returns `null`,whileunboxingto `T`throwsa `NullReferenceException`.¶¶¶¶Типrecord¶¶Recordscanbereferencetypesorvaluetypes.Theyallowcreatingimmutabletypesbyusingtheinitaccessoronproperties.¶Bydefault,arecordtypeoverridesmethodslike `Equals`, `GetHashCode`and `ToString`withvalue-basedimplementations,andtheyalsooverloadequality `==`andinequality `!=`operators.¶Youcanusethe `with`expressiontocreateanewrecordbasedonanexistingone:¶¶```csharp¶vartom =newPerson(\"Tom\", 37);¶varsam =tomwith [Name = \"Sam\" ];¶```¶¶Recordssupportdeconstruction,whichallowsyouunpacktheirvaluesintoseparatevariables,similartoJavaScript.¶Youcancreateapositionalrecord,whichautomaticallygeneratesaconstructoranddeconstructor.However,forstructrecords,positionalrecordsaremutablebydefault;tomakethepropertiesimmutable,youneedtoaddthe `readonly`modifierwithInitaccessor:¶¶```csharp¶publicrecordPerson(stringName,intAge); //That\'sall!¶publicreadonlyrecordstructPerson(stringName,intAge); //Nowpropertiesareautomaticallycreatedwithinit¶```¶¶¶¶Обобщения,преимуществаобобщений¶¶Genericsareamechanismforcodereuse,specificallyforreusingalgorithms.Adeveloperdescribesanalgorithmwithoutspecifyingtheexacttypeofobject,allowingthealgorithmworkwithdifferenttypes.¶¶Genericssupportreferencetypes,valuetypes,interfaces,delegates,methodsandinheritancerelationships.¶Atypeparametercanbeusedinproperties,indexers,events,constructors,destructors,andoperatormethods.¶¶Atypeparameterlike\'T\'isplaceholderinthegenericdefinition.¶Atypeargumentistheactualtypeinplaceofthetypeparameter.¶¶Advantagesofgenerics:¶-Typesafety.Ifyouuseawrongtypeyouwillgetacompile-timeerrororaruntimeexception.¶-Simplerandmorereadablecodebecauseyoudon\'tneedtocasttypes,makingthecodeeasierto