sExample<T>whereT :IComparable //typeparameterconstraint¶¶Interfaceconstraintsareefficientwithavaluetypebecausetheyavoidboxingwhenyoupassvaluetypeinstances.However,ifthetypeargumentisdeclaredasaninterface,boxingwilloccur.¶¶Theconstructorconstraint (new())makessurethetypeparameterisanon-abstracttypewithapublicparameterlessconstructor.Onlyoneconstructorconstraintcanbespecified.¶Youcannotcombinestructandnew()becauseeverystructalreadyhasapublicparameterlessconstructor,sospecifyingbothisredundant.¶¶¶¶Наследованиевклассах¶¶Inheritanceisalanguagemechanismthatallowsyoutodefineaderivedclassbasedonanexistingone,aswellasinherititsdataandbehavior.Aclasscanhaveonlyonedirectbaseclass,andthenewclasscanalsobeabaseclassforotherclasses.¶¶Aderivedclassinheritsalmostallmembersofthebaseclassexceptconstructors.Youcancallthebaseclassconstructorusingthebase(...)keyword.¶¶Thederivedclassinheritsallmethodsignaturesandtheirimplementationsfromthebaseclass.Derivedclassescanoverrideinheritedmembersthataremarkedas `virtual`inthebaseclass.Ifabaseclassmemberismarkedas `abstract`,itmustbeoverriddeninthederivedclass.¶¶Inheritanceappliestoclassesandinterfaces.Aclasscaninheritfromonebaseclassandimplementmanyinterfaces,butitmustimplementallthemethodsfromthoseinterfaces.Interfacesprovidealimitedformofmultipleinheritance.¶¶Classinheritanceallowsyoutosubstituteaninstanceofaderivedclasswhereverthebaseclassinstanceisexpected.Thisiscalledupcasting.¶¶¶¶Чтотакоеинтерфейсы.Наследованиеинтерфейсов.¶¶Aninterfaceisatypethatcontainsasetofmethodsignatures.Interfacesareusedtodefinebehaviorthatwillbeimplementedinaspecificclass.Ininterfaces,youcandefinestaticfields,staticpropertiesandstaticmethodsaswellasconstants,properties,events,indexersandmethods.StartingfromC# 8.0methodsandpropertiescanhavedefaultimplementation.¶¶Todefineaninterfaceusetheaccessmodifier (bydefault,itis `internal`)andthe `interface`keyword.Byconvention,interfacenamesbeginwithacapital \"I\".¶¶Aninterfacecaninheritfrommultipleinterfacesandaclassorstructmustimplementalltheirmethodsandpropertiesexceptthosewithdefaultimplementation.¶¶Implementedinterfacemembersmustbemarkedas `public`.¶¶Interfacesallowyoutosubstituteaninstancethatimplementstheinterfacewherevertheinterfacetypeisrequired.Thisenablescreateflexibleandlooselycoupledapplications,suchasDIcontainersormocktesting.¶¶TheCLRsupportsgenericinterfacesandgenericinterfacemethods.¶¶¶¶Модификаторыдоступа¶¶-publicmembersareaccessiblefromanycodeinanyassembly.¶¶-privatemembersareaccessibleonlyinsidethesameclassorinnestedtypesinsidethatclass.¶¶-protectedmembersareaccessiblewithinthesameclassandinderivedclasses.Thederivedclasscanbelocatedinanotherassembly.¶¶-internalmembersareaccessibleonlyinsidethesameassembly.¶¶-protectedinternalmembersareaccessiblewithinthesameassembly,orinderivedclassesinanotherassemblythroughavariableofthederivedclasstype.¶¶-privateprotectedmembersareaccessiblewithinthesameclass,orderivedclasseswithinthesameassembly.¶¶-filemembersareaccessibleonlywithinthesamefile.¶¶-Structscannotuseprotectedinternal,protectedorprivateprotectedmodifiersbecausestructscannotbeinherited.¶¶¶¶Явныеинеявныереализацииинтерфейсныхметодов¶¶4¶¶¶¶Обобщенныеинтерфейсы¶¶3¶¶¶¶Абстрактныйкласс¶¶Anabstractclassisaclassdeclaredwiththe `abstract`keyword.Thismeanstheclasscannotbeinstantiateddirectlyandisusedonlyasabaseclass.Itsmembersmayhavemissingorincompleteimplementations.¶¶Anabstractclasscaninheritfromabaseclassorimplementinterfaces,mappingtheirmemberstoabstractmembers.¶¶Itcancontainabstractmethods,properties,events,andindexersthatmustbeimplementedinderivedclasses.¶¶Abstractclassescanalsocontainfullyimplementedmembersandoverridevirtualmethods.¶¶Ifatleastonememberofaclassisabstract,theclassitselfmustbedefinedas `abstract`.¶¶¶¶Контравариантныеиковариантныеаргументы-типывделегатахиинтерфейсах¶¶Eachtypeparameterofagenericdelegateorinterfacemustbemarkedasinvariant,contravariant,orcovariant.Thisallowsyoutocastinstancesofagenericdelegateorinterfacetothesametypebutwithadifferenttypeparameter.¶¶Typeparameterscanbe:¶-Invariant -thetypeparametercannotbechanged,andthisapproachisusedbydefault.¶¶Contravariant —thetypeparametercanbeassignedfromamoregeneric (base)typetoamorespecific (derived)typeandismarkedwiththe `in`keyword.Itcanonlyappearininputpositions,suchasmethodparameters.Thisallowsyoutouseahandlerordelegatewithamoregeneric (base)typewhereamorespecific (derived)typeisexpectedasinput.¶¶MyAction<Animal>actAn = (o) =>o.Speak();¶MyAction<Dog>actDog =actAn;¶¶Covariant —thetypeparametercanbeassignedfromamorederivedtypetoalessderived (base)typeandismarkedwiththe\'out\'keyword.Itcanonlyappearinoutputpositions,suchasmethodreturntypes.Thisallowsyoutouseadalegateorinterfacewithmorederivedtypeswhereabasetypeisrequired.¶¶MyAction<Dog>getDog =GetDog;¶MyAction<Animal>getAnimal =getDog;¶¶Youcannotusevariancewiththe `ref`and `out`keywords.¶¶¶¶Символы¶¶ACharinthe .NETisavaluetypethatrepresentsaUTF-16Unicodecode.The `System.Char`typecontainstwopublicimmutablefields:theconstants `MinValue`and `MaxValue`.Thesefieldsshowthesmallestandlargestpossiblevalueforachar.¶¶¶¶Строки¶¶StringisanimmutablereferencetypethatrepresentsasequenceofUTF‑16characters.¶Strings = \"Hi\" + \" \" + \"there.\";¶¶Concatenationofliteralstringsisperformedatcompiletimeandtheresultisstoredinthemetadata.¶Concatenationofnon-literalstringsisperformedatruntime,allocationseveralstringsontheheap.So,itisbettertouse `StringBuilder`whenyouneedtojoinmanystrings.¶¶Tousestringinterpolation,useadollarsignbeforethestring,andusecurlybraces []asplaceholdersforvariablesorexpressions:¶`$\"Name: [name]Age: [age]\"`¶¶Touseaverbatimstringliteral,usethe\'at\'signbeforethestringtoavoidescapesequenceswhichishelpfulforfilepathsandregularexpressions:¶Stringfile = @\"C:\\Notepad.exe\";¶¶Touserawstringliteral (\"\"\"),usethreedoublequotes.Theyareusefulbecauseyoudon\'tneedescapesequencesforformatting.¶¶Stringsareimmutable,whichgivesbenefits,like:¶-Safecachingandsharingacrossthreads.¶-Value-basedcomparisonscheckthecontentsofthevalues,nottheirreferences.¶¶Stringpoolingisamechanismwhereeachuniquestringisstoredonlyonceinmemory.Ahashtableiscreatedwherethekeysarestringsandthevaluesarereferences.¶¶Stringinterningallowsyouaddnon-literalstringstothepoolbyhandusingspecialmethods:¶-StringIntern:Returnsareferencetothestring,addingittothepoolifitisnotalreadythere.¶-StringIsInterned:Returnsareferenceforstring,ornullifnot.¶¶¶¶StringBuilder¶¶StringBuilder,unlike `String`,isamutablesequenceofcharacters.Thismeansyoucanmodifyitscontentswithoutmakinganewobjectonthemanagedheap.¶¶`StringBuilder\'onlyallocatesmemoryfornewobjectsintwocases:¶-Whenthesizeisbiggerthanthecurrentcapacity;¶-Whenyoucallthe `ToString`methodtoconvertthe `StringBuilder`intoastringobject.¶¶Internally, `StringBuilder`isbasedonaChararray.Whenthestringbecomesbiggerthanthecurrentcapacity, `StringBuilder`automaticallyallocatesanewbiggerarrayandcopiesthecurrentcontenttoit.Thepreviousarraybecomeseligibleforgarbagecollection.¶¶¶¶Форматированиенесколькихобъектовводнустроку¶¶Strings =String.Format(\"On [0], [1]is [2]yearsold.\",newDateTime(2012, 4, 22, 14, 35, 5), \"Aida\", 9);¶¶¶¶Настраиваемыеатрибуты¶¶Customattributesallowyouaddextrainformationtoprogramelementsthatisstoredinthemetadataofamanagedmodule.¶¶Toapplyanattribute,useitsnameinsquarebracketsbeforeaclassoranothertypemember.¶Attributescanacceptparameters.¶Youcanapplyoneormoreattributestoanassembly,amodule,orspecificprogramelementssuchasclasses,interfaces,methods,properties,fields,parameters,andreturnvalues.¶¶Todefineacustomattributeclass,createaclassthatcomesfromtheabstractAttributeclassandhasapublicconstructor.¶¶¶¶Механикаобработкиисключений.try-catch-finally.throwexvsthrow.¶¶Thetryblockcontainscodethatcanthrowanexceptionorrequiresresourcecleanup.Recoverycodeisplacedinoneormorecatchblocks,andcleanupcodeisplacedinthefinallyblock.¶Atryblockmustmusthaveatleastonecatchblock,onefinallyblock,orboth.¶Tryblockscanbenested,andunhandledexceptionsarepassedtooutertryblock.¶¶Thecatchblockhandlesexceptions.¶Theexceptiontypeisspecifiedinparenthesesafterthecatchkeyword,andyoucanuseavariabletogetmoreinformationabouttheexception.¶Whenanexceptionoccurs,theprogramexecutionlooksforasuitablecatchblockinthecallstackfromthemostderivedexceptiontypestothebasetype,andfinally,toExceptionoratypelesscatchblock.¶Ifthereisnosuitablecatchblock,theprogramstopswithanerror.¶¶Whenasuitablecatchblockisfound,youcanchoosearecoverystrategy:¶-Rethrowthesameexceptionwith `throw`,whichkeepsthestacktrace;¶-Rethrowwith `throwex`,toresetthestacktraceandhidesensitivedetails;¶-Throwadifferentexceptiontypewith `thrownewSomeException;`¶-Completehandlingandcontinueexecutioninthefinallyblockorafterit.¶¶Ifnoexceptionisthrowninthetryblock,allcatchblocksareskippedandtheprogramproceedstothefinallyblock,ifitisthere.¶¶Exceptionfilters (whenclause)allowyoutohandleexceptionsbasedonacondition.¶¶Thefinallyblockalwaysexecutesandperformscleanupafterthetryblock,forexample,closingafile.Itshouldbeplacedafterallcatchblocks,ordirectlyafterthetryblock.¶¶¶¶Созданиепользовательскихисключений.¶¶5¶¶¶¶Вочторазворачиваютсяблокиlock,usingиforeach¶¶Whenyouusethelock,using,andforeachstatements,thecompilerautomaticallygeneratestry/finallyblocks.Itdoesthesamewhenyoudefineadestructor (~Type),whichcompilestoanoverrideofFinalize.¶Whenworkingwiththeseconstructs,thecodeyouwriteisplacedinsideatryblock,andthecleanupcodeisplacedinthefinallyblock.Specifically:¶-lock:thefinallyblockreleasesthelock (Monitor.Exit).¶-using:thefinallyblockcallsDisposeontheobject.¶-foreach:thefinallyblockcallsDisposeontheIEnumerator (ifitimplementsIDisposable).¶¶-destructor (~Type):thefinallyblockcallsbase.Finalize().¶¶¶¶Корректноевосстановлениепослеисключения¶¶7¶¶¶¶КакаяразницамеждуметодамиFinalizeиDispose.Чемплохдеструктор/финализаторикогдаиспользоватьIDisposable?¶¶Finalize (finalizer)isusedtoexplicitlyreleaseunmanagedresourceswhenthegarbagecollectorruns.UnmanagedresourcesareobjectsnotmanagedbyGCandnotpartof .NET,suchasdatabaseconnections,networkconnections,fileorsockethandles.¶¶Todefinefinalizer,useaconstructorsyntax,butwithatilde (`~`)beforename.However,duringcleanuptheGCcallstheFinalizemethod,notthedestructordirectly.AdrawbackofusingfinalizersisthatyoudonotknowexactlywhenorwhatordertheGCwillremovetheobjectfrommemory.¶¶Dispose (`IDisposable.Dispose`)isusedtoexplicitlyreleaseunmanagedresourcesbythedeveloperorwiththe `using`statement.¶¶TodefineDisposemethod,theobjectmustimplementthe `IDisposable`interface.Disposemethodmustbecalledmultipletimeswithouterror.`IDisposable`objectscanbereleasedwiththe `using`statement,whichthecompilerturnsintoatry/finallythatcallsDisposeautomatically.¶¶Thedifferencebetweenusing `Finalize`and `Dispose`isthat `Finalize`iscalledbytheGC,andyoudon\'tknowexactlywhenthiswillhappen,while `Dispose`methodcanbecalledexplicitlybythedeveloperassoonascleanupisnecessary,orby `using`statement.¶¶¶¶Сборщикмусора.Триггерывызова.Чтовлияетнаегоскоростьработы.Количествопоколений.LOH.КакопределитьпроизводительностьGC.ЧтотакоеPOH.¶¶TheGarbageCollector (GC)managesmemoryallocationanddeallocationforanapplication.Itistriggeredwhen:¶-Thereisnospaceleftintheheaptocreateanewobjectinanygeneration;¶-TheOSsignalsalackoffreememory;¶-TheCLRisshutdownoranAppDomainisunloaded;¶-Thestaticmethod `GC.Collect()`iscalled.¶¶Duringthegarbagecollectionprocess,theGCstartsfromtherootelements,andmarksallreachableobjectsinthecallstack.Unmarkedobjectsareremoved,whilemarkedobjectsarecompacted (defragmented)andpromotedtothenextgeneration.Therearethreegenerationsintotal,whichwasfoundexperimentallyanditisconsideredoptimal.¶¶InadditiontotheSmallObjectHeap (SOH),thereisLargeObjectHeapstoresobjectslargerthan 85KB.Itisnotcompactedandbelongstogeneration 2.¶¶ThePinnedObjectHeap (POH)isusedforexplicitlypinnedobjectstopreventdefragmentationanditisavailabletodevelopers.POHonlysupportspinnedarrays.¶¶Thesedays,bothPOHandLOHbelongtotheUserOldHeap (UOH).¶¶Tomonitorperformance,therearestaticmethodssuchas:¶- `CollectionCount` —returnsthenumberofcollectionsforaspecifiedgeneration;¶- `GetTotalMemory` —returnsthetotalallocatedmemory.¶¶¶¶Потокиипроцессы.Ихразличия.Переключенияконтекста.backgroundиforegroundthread¶¶ThreadsandprocessesperformparallelexecutionoftasksinanOS.Thisimprovesperformanceandpreventsthewholesystemfrombeingblockedifanexceptionoccurs.¶¶Aprocessisaninstanceofaprogramwithitsownresourcesandvirtualaddressspace.Processesareisolatedfromeachother,sooneprocesscannotaffectanother.¶¶Athreadisaunitofexecutionthatusestheresourcesofitsprocess.¶¶Dataexchangebetweenthreadswithinthesameprocessisfasterthanbetweenseparateprocesses.Ifathreadentersaninfiniteloop,onlythatthreadisblocked,nottheentiresystem.¶¶ContextswitchingletsthesystemshareCPUtimeamongthreads.Itimprovesresponsivenessandreliability,butmayreduceperformanceduetoswitchingoverhead.¶¶Foregroundandbackgroundthreads:¶-Aforegroundthreadisanactivethreadthatkeepsanapprunning;whenallforegroundthreadsfinish,allrunningbackgroundthreadsarestopped,andtheapplicationexits.¶¶Bydefault,themainthreadandthreadscreatedviatheThreadclassareforegroundthreads,whilethreadsfromthethreadpoolarebackgroundthreads.', 1);
