(5, 1, 5, 1, 'Способысозданияпотоков.¶¶Firstmethod.The `Thread`classallowsyoutocreateathreadmanually.Itreceivesa `ThreadStart`delegateinitsconstructor,thanyoucallthe `Start()`methodtorunthethread.Threadscreatedthiswayareforegroundthreadsbydefault.Themaindrawbackisthateachnewthreadrequiresadditionalresources,whichcanreduceperformance.¶¶Secondmethod:TheThreadPoolisasetofreusablethreadsmanagedbytheCLR.Whenarequestcomesin,itisputintoaqueue.The `ThreadPool`takesrequestsfromthequeueandassignsthemtoavailablethreadsforexecution.Ifnothreadsareavailable,theThreadPoolcancreateanewthread.Aftercompletingitstask,thethreadreturnstothepoolforreuse.Thisimprovesperformance;however,whentherearemanyrequests,additionalthreadsmaybecreated.Theseextrathreadsself-terminateandfreeresourcesastheloaddecreases.¶¶Eachprocesshasasinglethreadpool.¶Youcansetthesizeofthethreadpoolwith `ThreadPool.SetMaxThreads`.¶Allthreadpoolarebackgroundthreads.¶¶Advantages:¶-Youdon\'tneedtocreateanewthreadforeachtaskmanually,improvingapplicationperformance.¶-Thethreadpoolmanagesthreadcreationautomatically.¶¶Limitations:¶-Youcannotsetthepriority,getthethread\'sname,getareturnvalue,orbenotifiedwhenthetaskiscomplete.¶-Itissuitableonlyforshort-livedtasks,sincealargenumberofblockedthreadscanpreventnewtasksfromstarting.¶¶Thirdmethod: `Task`representsanasynchronousunitofworkmanagedbythethreadpool,butcanalsoberunsynchronously.¶Tocreatea `Task`,youpassan `Action`delegateoralambdaandstartwiththe `Start()`methodorTast.Run.Forreturnvalues,use `Task<TResult>`andthe `Result`property.¶¶¶¶Концепцияасинхронности,TAP.Асинхронныеметоды.Какиеоперациилучшевыполнятьсинхронно,акакиеасинхронно.¶¶Asynchronymeansperforminganoperationwithoutwaitingforittocompleteandblockingthemainthread,allowingthesystemtoperformothertaskswhilealong-runningoperation (suchasanetworkrequestordiskI/O)isinprogress.¶¶TodefineAsynchronousmethod,usethe `async`keyword,whichallowsyoutousethe `await`keywordinsidethemethod.Whenthecodereachesan `await`expressionthethreadreturnstothepoolandcandoothertasks.Themethodcontinueexecutingwhentheawaitedtaskisfinished.¶¶Returntypesforasynchronousmethods:¶- `Task<TResult>` -formethodsthatreturnavalue;¶- `Task` -formethodsthatdonotreturnavalue;¶- `IAsyncEnumerable<T>` -forasynchronousstreams,allowingiterationoverelementsproducedasynchronously;¶- `void` -foreventhandlersandexceptionsthrowninthesemethodsgenerallycannotbecaughtexternally.¶¶Anasynchronousmethodcannothave `out`, `ref`,or `in`parameters,butitcancallmethodswiththeseparameters.¶Asyncmethodnameshouldendwith \"Async\"andhaveanoverloadthatacceptsa `CancellationToken`.¶The `await`operatorcanbeusedwithina `try`block,butnotwithin `catch`, `finally`,or `unsafe`blocks.¶¶Use `async/await`onlyforalongtasks,suchasnetworkrequests,fileordatabaseaccess,oruserinput.¶¶¶¶ВочторазворачиваетсякомпиляторомконструкцияawaitиTask?¶¶The `async/await`constructistransformedbythecompilerintoastatemachine.Inthisstatemachinethemethod\'svariablesbecomefields,whichallowsthemethodtorememberitsstateandresumeexecutionafterwaitingforalong-runningoperationtocomplete.¶¶`Task`buildsacontinuationchain,whichgrowsaccordingtothenumberoftaskslinkedsequentially,andthesystem\'sstateismanagedthroughclosuresgeneratedbythecompiler.¶¶¶¶CPU-boundиIO-Boundоперации¶¶CPU-boundoperationsconsumetheresourcesofthecurrentprocessor.IftherearetoomanyCPU-boundoperationsrunningatonce,theCPUcanbecomeoverloaded,whichreducesefficiency,sincetheoperatingsystemmustfrequentlyswitchbetweenthreads,whichslowsdownexecution.¶¶Incontrast,I/O-boundoperationscanberunasynchronouslyandareexecutedoutsidethecurrentprocessor,sotheydonotdirectlyloadtheCPU.¶¶Therefore,runningalargenumberofI/O-boundtasksusuallydoesnotreduceprocessorperformance.¶¶¶¶Контекстсинхронизации.ConfigureAwait(false)vsConfigureAwait(true)vsбезиспользованияConfigureAwait.¶¶1¶¶¶¶ЧтотакоеCancellationToken?Отменаасинхронныхопераций.¶¶2¶¶¶¶Видысинхронизациипотоков.lock,Monitor¶¶Thelockoperatorisasimplifiedsyntaxtousethe `Monitor`class.Itdefinesabl