anewreference: `List =newList<T>();`¶¶Comparisonof `List<KeyValuePair<TKey,TValue>>`and `Dictionary<TKey,TValue>`:¶¶List<KeyValuePair<TKey,TValue>>:¶-Lighterdatastructure.Doesnotrequirehashcalculations.¶-Insertionisfastersinceelementsarejustappendedtotheendofthelistwithoutcalculatingahash.¶-Linearsearch. -Canbeserializedusingthestandard `XMLSerializer`.¶-Updatingakey/valuepairisnotpossibledirectly;youneedtoremovetheexistingpairandaddanewone.¶¶Dictionary<TKey,TValue>:¶-Heavierstructure,asitusesahashtable.¶-Insertionisslowerduetohashcalculationandpossiblecollisionresolution.¶-LookupisclosetoO(1)thankstohashing.¶-Requirescustomcodeforserialization.¶-Valuescanbeupdateddirectlybykey.¶¶¶¶LinkedList.Преимуществаинедостатки.¶¶Alinkedlistconsistsofconnectednodes,eachnodestoringdata (`Value`)andareferencetothenextnode (`Next`).Itisoptimizedforinsertionanddeletionbutisslowforindexingandsearching.¶Methods:¶-AddLast —addsanelementtotheendofthelist:¶ -Ifa `tail`pointerisstored,complexityisO(1);ifnot,O(n).¶-AddFirst —addsanelementtothebeginningofthelist.Complexity:O(1)¶-Remove —removesanelement.Complexity:O(n)¶-Contains —checksifanelementexists.Complexity:O(n)¶-Clear —removesallreferences.¶-IEnumerable —canbeimplementedtoallowiterationwitha `foreach`loop.¶¶¶¶Двусвязныйсписок,Кольцевойодносвязныйсписок,Кольцевойдвусвязныйсписок,¶¶Adoublylinkedlistconsistsofasequenceofnodes,whereeachnodecontainsdata (thevalueoftheelement),areferencetothenextnode (`Next`),andareferencetothepreviousnode (`Previous`).¶Acircularsinglylinkedlistisalinkedlistinwhichthelastelementcontainsareferencetothefirstelement,makingthelistcircular.¶Acirculardoublylinkedlistisacircularlistwhereeachnodecontainsbothapointertothepreviousnodeandapointertothenextnode.¶¶¶¶Stack,Queue,Dequeue,PriorityQueue¶¶AstackworksaccordingtotheLIFOprinciple (LastIn -FirstOut).Thelastelementaddedwillbethefirstoneremoved.¶-Pushaddsanobject —O(1)¶-Popremovesandreturnsanobject —O(1)¶-Peekreturnsthetopelementwithoutremovingit —O(1)¶¶AqueueworksaccordingtotheFIFOprinciple (FirstIn -FirstOut).Thefirstaddedelementwillbethefirstonetoberemoved.¶-Enqueueaddsanelementtotheendofthequeue¶-Dequeueremovesandreturnstheelementfromthebeginningofthequeue¶-Peekreturnsthefrontelementwithoutremovingit —O(1)¶Adeque (double-endedqueue)isusedwhenelementsneedtobeaddedorremovedfrequentlyfrombothendsofthequeue.Itisnotimplementeddirectlyin .NET,butyoucanuse,forexample, `LinkedList<T>`,whichprovidesequivalentfunctionality.¶ApriorityqueueworkssimilarlytoFIFObutallowsassigningaprioritywhenaddingelements.ElementswithlowerpriorityareprocessedfirstinFIFOorder,andthiscontinuesuntilelementswiththelowestprioritylevelareprocessed.¶-Enqueue(element,priority) —addsanelementwiththespecifiedpriority.¶-Dequeue() —removesandreturnstheelementwiththehighestpriority.¶-Peek() —returnstheelementwiththehighestprioritywithoutremovingit.¶Thesedatastructuresareveryefficientwhenyouonlyneedtoworkwiththeendsofthedata,andthemiddleelementsarenotimportant.¶¶¶¶BinaryHeap,BinarySearchTree,АВЛ-дерева,Обходыдерева,Балансировкаузлов¶¶Abinaryheapisatreewhereeachnodehasatmosttwochildrenandalllevelsarecompletelyfilled.¶¶Supportstwovariants:¶Max-heap:Eachnode\'skey ≥itschildren\'skeys.¶Min-heap:Eachnode\'skey ≤itschildren\'skeys.¶Complexity:¶-Readtop-priorityelement:O(1)¶-Insertionandextraction:O(logn)¶-Sorting:O(nlogn)¶¶Balancingisperformedbyswappingtherootelementwithoneofitschildrenuntiltheheappropertyisrestored.Whenremovinganelement,itisreplacedwiththelastaddedelement,whichisthenbalanced.¶Formulas:¶-Leftchild: 2i + 1¶-Rightchild: 2i + 2¶-Parent: (i - 1) / 2¶¶Abinarysearchtree (BST)isabinarytreewhereeachnodehasuptotwochildren.Nodesintheleftsubtreearesmallerthantheparentnode,andnodesintherightsubtreearegreaterorequalthantheparentnode.Elementswithnochildrenarecalledleaves.Theonewithnoparentistheroot.¶Complexity:¶-Search,Insert,Delete:O(logn)¶¶AnAVLtreeisabinarysearchtreethatisbalancedsothattheheightsoftheleftandrightsubtreesforanynodedifferbynomorethan 1.¶¶Treetraversals:¶-Pre-order: 1 -currentnode ; 2 -leftnode ; 3 -rightnode (usedforcopyingthetree).¶-Post-order: 1 -leftnode ; 2 -rightnode ; 3 -currentnode (usedfordeletion).¶-In-order: 1 -leftnode ; 2 -currentnode ; 3 -rightnode (usedforsorting).¶¶¶¶Hashtable,Hashset,Хэш-функция,Dictionary,коллизия¶¶AHashtableisadatastructurethatstoresdataofdifferenttypesaskey-valuepairs.Itusesahashfunctiontocalculateanumber(hashcode)basedonthegivenkey,whichisusedasanindex.TheadvantageofhashingisthatitprovidesO(1)timecomplexityforoperations,regardlessofthesizeofthestructure.¶¶Eachkeymustbeuniqueinthehashtableandcannotbenull.However,thevaluecanbe `null`orduplicated.¶Ahashfunctionmustreturnthesamehashcodeforthesameinput.Itshouldalsodistributekeysevenlyacrosstheentirerange,andthefasteritcomputesthevalue,thebetter.¶¶Hashcollisionsoccurwhenthefunctionreturnsthesamenumberfortwodifferentkeys.¶Toresolvecollisions,asinglylinkedlistiscreatedtostorethekeys,butinthiscase,thecomplexityincreasestoO(n).¶¶Thetypeusedasakeymustoverrideboth `GetHashCode()`and `Equals()`:¶-Equals()`isusedtocomparedictionarykeys;¶Ifcollisionoccursthedictionarycheckstwokeys,forequivalencebycalling `A.Equals(B)`.¶¶HashSet<T>isadatastructurebasedonahashtable,butitstoresonlyuniqueelementsofaspecifictype.¶¶Dictionaryisadatastructurealsobasedonahashtable,wheredataisstoredaskey-valuepairs,butunlike `Hashtable`, `Dictionary`mustbestronglytypedduringinitialization.¶¶¶¶SortedList,SortedSet,SortedDictionary¶¶SortedList<TKey,TValue>isadatastructurebasedonanarray,whereallelementsaresortedbykey.Itusesbinarysearchtomaintainorderingandtosearchforelements.¶¶SortedSet<T>isadatastructurebasedonared-blacktree,butitstoresonlyuniqueelementsofthesametypeinasortedorder.¶¶TheSortedDictionary<TKey,TValue>classisadatastructurebasedonared-blacktree,whereallelementsaresortedbykey.¶¶SortedListuseslessmemorythan `SortedDictionary`and `SortedSet`,buttheyarefasterforinsertingandremovingelements,whilesearchperformanceisthesame:O(log₂(n)).¶¶InsertionDeletionSearch¶SortedList<TKey,TValue>O(n)O(n)O(log2(n))¶SortedDictionary<TKey,TValue>O(log2(n))O(log2(n))O(log2(n))¶SortedSet<T>O(log2(n))O(log2(n))O(log2(n))¶¶¶¶ЧтотакоеLINQ.КакреализованыосновныеметодыLinqподкапотом.СкакимиколлекциямиможноиспользоватьLinq?¶¶LINQ (Language-IntegratedQuery)isaquerylanguageforvarioustypesofdatasourcesthatsupportthe `IEnumerable<T>`or `IQueryable<T>`interfaces,suchascollectionsordatabaseslikeSQL.¶¶ALINQqueryconsistsofthreeactions:thedatasource,thequerydefinition,andthequeryexecution.It\'simportanttounderstandthatqueryexecutionisdeferreduntilthequeryvariableisprocessedina `foreach`statementorexplicitlycalledusingmethodslike `ToList`, `ToArray`,oraggregatemethodssuchas `Count`, `Max`, `Average`,and `First`.¶¶LINQsupportstwotypesofsyntax,whichcanbecombined:querysyntaxandmethodsyntax.¶```csharp¶varres =fromninMyArray¶wheren > 0¶selectn;¶IEnumerable<int>numQuery2 =numbers.Where(num =>num % 2 == 0).OrderBy(n =>n);¶```¶¶LINQmethodsareimplementedasextensionmethods,soyoucaneasilyaddyourown.Mostofthesemethodstakealambdaexpressionordelegateasaparameter.¶¶ForimplementingLINQprovidersforexternaldatasources,the `IQueryable<T>`interfaceisusedalongwithasetofextensionmethodsthatarealmostidenticaltothoseavailablefor `IEnumerable<T>`.Because `List<T>`implements `IEnumerable<T>`,and `DbSet<T>`fromEntityFrameworkimplements `IQueryable<T>`,queriesareexecuteddifferently.¶Themaindifferencewithextensionmethodsfor `IQueryable<T>`isthattheydonotcontaindataprocessinglogic.Instead,theybuildanexpressiontreethatispassedtotheproviderwhichthentranslatesthequeryintothelanguageofthedatasourceitworkswithandexecutesit.¶¶¶¶КакработаетсравнениетиповчерезReferenceEquals,Equalsи ==вReferenceTypeиValueTypeчерезEquals.¶¶Forreferencetypes, `ReferenceEquals`, `Equals`,and `==`compareobjectreferencesontheheapandreturn `true`ifthereferencesareequal.However, `Equals`and `==`canbeoverriddentocomparebyvalue.Thedefaultimplementationof `Equals`internallycalls `ReferenceEquals`.¶¶Thestaticmethod `Equals(ObjectobjA,ObjectobjB)`firstcheckstheobjectreferencesusing `==`,thencheckseachobjectfor `null`,andfinallycallsthestandardvirtualmethod `a.Equals(b)`.¶¶Forvaluetypes, `Equals`and `==`compareobjectsbyvalue,butifastructcontainsfieldsthatarereferencetypes,youshouldoverridethem,aswellas `GetHashCode`,sincethiscanimproveperformance.¶¶varobj1 =newTestClass [Count = 2];¶varobj2 =newTestClass [Count = 2];¶Console.WriteLine(obj1 ==obj2);false¶Console.WriteLine(obj1.Equals(obj2));false -Equalsisnotoverridden.¶Console.WriteLine(object.ReferenceEquals(obj1,obj2));false¶Console.WriteLine(obj1.Equals(obj2));true -Equalsisoverridden.¶¶¶¶Правилареализацииоператораравенства (==),IComparableиметодаEquals.ПримерыреализацийметодаEquals(Object)¶¶Whenimplementingtheequalityoperator (`==`)orthe `IComparable`interface,youshouldalsoimplementthe `Equals`method.¶¶Whenimplementingthe `CompareTo`methodofthe `IComparable`interface,itisalsorecommendedtooverloadtheoperators `==`, `!=`, `<`,and `>`.¶¶Ifyouoverridethe `Equals`method,youmustalsooverride `GetHashCode`.¶¶Donotthrowexceptionsfromthe `Equals`and `GetHashCode`methodsorfromtheequalityoperator (`==`).¶¶Examplesofimplementingthe `Equals(Object)`method:¶-Checkiftheobjectis `null`,comparetheobjecttypes,explicitlycasttothecurrentclasstype,andcompareitsfieldswiththecorrespondingfieldsoftheinputobject.¶¶-Usethe `is`operator: `if (objisTestClassobjectType)`,thencomparethefieldsinside.¶¶-Usethe `as`operator:Implementthe `IEquatable<T>`interface;inthefirstmethod,return `Equals(objasImaginaryNumber)`,andinthesecond `Equals`method,checkfor `null`andcomparethefields.¶¶¶¶СравнениеспомощьювспомогательныхклассовиинтерфейсовIComparable,IComparer,IEqualityComparer,IEquatable¶¶IComparable<T>definesthe `CompareTo`method,whichisusedtocomparethecurrentobjectwithanotherobjectofthesametype.Themethodreturnsaninteger,soyoushouldalsooverloadthecomparisonoperators:¶-Lessthanzero:currentobjectislessthanthespecifiedobject;¶-Zero:objectsareequal;¶-Greaterthanzero:c