ingleResponsibilityPrinciple -aclassshouldhaveonlyonereasontochange;itmustberesponsibleforonlyonespecifictask.Allitsfunctionalityshouldbecohesiveandtighlyrelated.¶¶Open/ClosedPrinciple -entitiesshouldbeopenforextensionbutclosedformodification.¶¶LiskovSubstitutionPrinciple (LSP) —subtypemustbesubstitutableforitsbasetypewithoutalteringprogramcorrectness:¶-Preconditionscannotbestrengthenedinasubclass.Theyappearattheverybeginningofamethod,andonlypublicproperties,fields,ormethodparameterscanbeusedaspreconditions.¶-Postconditionscannotbeweakenedinasubclass.Theyappearattheveryendofamethod,beforethereturnstatement.¶-Invariants —allconditionsofthebaseclassmustalsobepreservedinthesubclass.Forexample,afieldlike `Age`thatmustnotexceed 100shouldmaintainthisruleinbothpropertiesandmethods.¶¶InterfaceSegregationPrinciple —It\'sbettertouseseveralsmall,specializedinterfacesratherthanonelarge,general-purposeinterface.Thisallowsclientstodependonlyontheinterfacestheyactuallyneed.¶¶DependencyInversionPrinciple —High-levelmodulesshouldnotdependonlow-levelmodules;bothshoulddependonabstractions;abstractionsshouldnotdependondetails;detailsshoulddependonabstractions.Thisprinciplehelpscreatelooselycoupledentitiesthatareeasytotest,modify,andupdate.¶¶¶¶Другиепринципы:DRY,KISS,YAGNI,DAMP,AAA.¶¶Don\'tRepeatYourself /DuplicationIsEvil (DRY/DIE) —duplicatecodeshouldbeextractedintoaseparatemethod.¶¶KeepItSimple,Stupid! (KISS) —makethearchitectureassimpleandunderstandableaspossible,usingdesignpatternsandnotreinventingthewheel.¶¶YouAin\'tGonnaNeedIt (YAGNI) —don\'taddfunctionalityuntilitisactuallyneeded.¶¶DescriptiveAndMeaningfulPhrases (DAMP) —writeunittestssothatwhathappensinthemcanbeunderstoodwithoutadditionalcommentsordocumentation.ThisisachievedbyusingdescriptivenamesandallowsforsmallviolationsoftheDRYprinciplewhennecessary.¶¶ArrangeActAssert (AAA) —aruleforcreatingunittests:setuptheconditions (Arrange),performtheaction (Act),andchecktheresult (Assert).¶¶¶¶Другиепринципы:GRASP.¶¶**GRASP (GeneralResponsibilityAssignmentSoftwarePatterns)**isasetofprinciplesthatdefinehowresponsibilitiesshouldbedistributedamongclassesinanapplication:¶- **InformationExpert** —theclassthathasthemostnecessaryinformationtoperformataskshouldberesponsibleforexecutingthattask.Forexample,if `Account`storesaccountinformation,itshouldprovidetheaccountstatement.¶- **Creator** —classesthatcreateotherclasses.Thiscanbeafactory,apool,etc.¶- **Controller** —anobjectthatcarriesoutcontrolfunctions,responsibleforhandlingincomingrequestsanddecidingwhichobjectsshouldexecutethem.Example:theControllerintheMVCpattern.¶- **LowCoupling** —codeshouldbewrittenbasedoninterfacesandabstractionsratherthanspecificimplementations.¶- **HighCohesion** —methodswithinaclassshouldbecloselyrelatedtoeachother.¶- **PureFabrication** —classesthatdonotrepresentreal-worldobjectsfromtheapplication\'sdomain.Forexample,aserviceorrepositorythatretrievesandsavessuchobjectstoadatabase.¶- **Indirection** —usingintermediaryobjectstoreducedirectdependenciesbetweenclasses,forexample,usingthemediatorpattern.ThecontrollerinMVCactsasanintermediarybetweentheModelandtheView.¶- **ProtectedVariations** —identifyobjectsthataremostlikelytochangeandapplymeasurestominimizetheimpactofthesechangesontherestoftheapplication.¶- **Polymorphism** —theabilityofobjectswiththesamespecificationtohavedifferentimplementations.Inthiscontext,theprincipleiscloselyrelatedtotheGoFStrategypattern.¶¶¶¶IoC,DI,Способыполучениязависимостей,IoC-контейнер,ПреимуществаDI¶¶InversionofControl (IoC)isaprincipleforwritinglooselycoupledcode.Accordingtothisprinciple,objectsdonotmanagetheirowndependencies,butreceivethemfromtheoutside.Forexample,thiscanbedonethroughaggregationofaninterface,abstract,orbaseclass.AnIoCcontainerhelpsprovidetherequireddependencies.¶¶DependencyInjection (DI)isoneimplementationofthisprinciple.Whenadependentclassdoesnotcreateinstancesofotherclassesitself,butreceivesthemduringitsinitialization,theresponsibilityforcreatingtheseclassesisdelegatedtoathird