tartingwithavalue;inthemiddle —stringsstartingandendingwithspecificvalues.¶- `_` —representsanysinglecharacter.¶ ...WHEREemailLIKE\'%@hotmail.%\' //Searchforemailswiththehotmaildomain¶ ...WHEREполе_таблицыLIKE\'begin%end\'; //Stringstartswith \"begin\"andendswith \"end\"¶ ...WHEREполе_таблицыLIKE\'_ext\' //Stringoflength 4,lastthreeare \"ext\"¶¶ESCAPEisusedwhenyouneedtotreatspecialcharactersasliteralsorusing `\\`beforeit:¶ ...WHEREprogressLIKE\'3!%\'ESCAPE\'!\'; //Searchforprogressequalto \"3%\"¶¶¶¶ОператорORDERBY,GROUPBY,Агрегатныефункции,HAVING¶¶ORDERBYisusedtosortresults,where `ASC`sortsinascendingorder (default),and `DESC`sortsindescendingorder.Tosortresultsbytwoormorecolumns,listthemseparatedbycommas:¶SELECTtable_fieldsFROMtable_nameWHERE ...ORDERBYcolumn_1 [ASC |DESC],column_2 [ASC |DESC];¶¶GROUPBYisusedtogrouprecordsbyspecifiedcolumns.Inthequery,youcanuseonlyliterals,aggregatefunctions,andfieldsthatarepartofthegrouping.AllNULLvaluesareconsideredequalandfallintoonegroup.¶SELECTgrouping_field,aggregate_functionFROMtable_nameGROUPBYgrouping_field;¶¶HAVINGisusedtofilteralreadygroupeddata.Unlike `WHERE`,whichfiltersrows, `HAVING`isappliedaftergrouping.¶SELECThome_type,AVG(price)asavg_priceFROMRoomsGROUPBYhome_typeHAVINGavg_price > 50¶¶Aggregatefunctionsperformcalculationsonasetofvaluesandreturnasinglevalue.AggregatefunctionsignoreNULLvalues,exceptfor `COUNT(*)`.¶SELECThome_type,AVG(price)asavg_priceFROMRoomsGROUPBYhome_type¶- `SUM(column)` —Returnsthesumofvalues¶- `AVG(column)` —Returnstheaveragevalue¶- `COUNT(column)` —Returnsthenumberofrecords¶- `MIN(column)` —Returnstheminimumvalue¶- `MAX(column)` —Returnsthemaximumvalue¶- `FLOOR()` —Roundsdowntothenearestinteger¶¶¶¶ПорядоквыполненияSQLзапроса¶¶Whycan\'tweuseWHEREtofiltergroupedresultsandwhydoweneedaseparateoperator (HAVING)?¶It\'sallabouttheorderofexecutionofanSQLquery:¶¶1.FROMtable_name —retrievesdatafromtables,performsjoinsandsubqueriesifspecified.¶¶2.WHERErow_conditions —filtersrowsthatshouldnotparticipateinfurtherprocessing.¶¶3.GROUPBYgrouping_columns —groupsthefilteredrowsbasedonspecifiedcolumns.¶¶4.HAVINGconditions_on_grouped_rows —filtersthealreadygroupeddata (thisiswhyitexistsseparatelyfrom `WHERE`).¶¶5.SELECT [constants,aggregate_functions,grouping_columns] —onlynowisthe `SELECT`commandapplied.Atthisstage,thespecifiedcolumns,aggregatefunctions,andgroupingfieldsfrompreviousstepsareselected.¶¶6.ORDERBYsort_condition —sortsthefinalresult,whichcanincludeordinarycolumns,aggregatefunctions,orevenwindowfunctionsiftheyareused.¶¶7.LIMIT /OFFSET /FETCH —skipsanumberofrowsfromthesortedresultset.¶¶¶¶ВидымноготабличныхзапросовJOIN.ВнутреннеесоединениеINNERJOIN¶¶Ajoincanbe:INNER (default)orOUTER.OuterjoinsaredividedintoLEFT,RIGHT,andFULL.The `ON`clauseisusedtomatchtablestoeachothersothatthejoinworks.¶¶SELECTtable_fieldsFROMleft_table¶[INNER] | [[LEFT |RIGHT |FULL][OUTER]]JOINright_table¶ONjoin_condition¶[INNER] | [[LEFT |RIGHT |FULL][OUTER]]JOINtable_n¶ONjoin_condition¶¶INNERJOINisajointhatreturnspairsofrecordsfrombothtablesthatsatisfythejoincondition.¶¶FROMPaymentsINNERJOINGoodsONPayments.good_id =Goods.good_id¶¶InsteadofusingINNERJOIN,youcanalsousetheWHEREclause.Forexample,joiningtablesbyacommonfieldgood_idwillreturntablethatcontainsrecordswiththesamegood_idvalue:¶¶SELECTfamily_member,member_nameFROMPayments,FamilyMembers¶WHEREPayments.family_member =FamilyMembers.member_id¶¶¶¶ВнешнеесоединениеOUTERJOIN,Внешнеелевоесоединение (LEFTOUTERJOIN)Внешнееправоесоединение (RIGHTOUTERJOIN)Внешнееполноесоединение (FULLOUTERJOIN)¶¶OUTERJOIN (ExternalJoin)¶Anouterjoincanbeofthreetypes:LEFT,RIGHT,andFULL (bydefault).Themaindifferencebetweenanouterjoinandaninnerjoinisthatitalwaysreturnsallrowsfromone (LEFT,RIGHT)orbothtables (FULL).¶¶LEFTOUTERJOIN -returnsallvaluesfromthelefttablewithmatchingvaluesfromtherighttablethatsatisfythejoincondition,orreplacesthemwithNULLifthereisnomatch.¶SELECTcolumns¶FROMleft_table¶LEFTJOINright_table¶ONright_table.key =left_table.key;¶¶Togetrowsthatexistonlyinthelefttable,use:¶WHEREright_table.keyISNULL¶¶RIGHTOUTERJOIN -returnsallvaluesfromtherighttablewithmatchingvaluesfromthelefttablethatsatisfythejoincondition,orreplacesthemwithNULLifthereisnomatch.¶SELECTcolumns¶FROMleft_table¶RIGHTJOINright_table¶ONright_table.key =left_table.key;¶Togetrowsthatexistonlyintherighttable,use:¶WHEREleft_table.keyISNULL¶¶FULLOUTERJOIN -returnsrecordsfrombothtablesbyperforminganinnerjoinandthenincludingtheunmatchedrowsfromtheleftandrightouterjoins.Unmatchedvalueswillbe `NULL`.¶SELECTcolumns¶FROMleft_table¶FULLOUTERJOINright_table¶ONright_table.key =left_table.key;¶¶FULLJOINisnotimplementedinallDBMSs,butyoucanemulateitusing:¶LEFTJOIN =>UNIONALL =>RIGHTJOIN =>WHEREleft_table.keyISNULL¶¶¶¶Ограничениевыборки,операторLIMIT,TOP,OFFSETFETCH¶¶LIMITisanoperatorusedtorestrictthenumberofreturnedrows.Ifyoudonotspecifythenumberofrowstoskip,countingstartsfromthebeginningofthetable.¶SELECTcolumnsFROMtable_listLIMIT [offset,]row_count;¶¶TheLIMIToperatorisnotimplementedinallDBMSs.Forexample,inMSSQL,the `TOP`operatorisusedtoreturnrecordsfromthebeginningofthetable,andwhenyouneedtoskiprecords,the `OFFSETFETCH`clauseisused.¶¶Todisplayrows 3to 5,youcanusethefollowingquery:¶SELECT *FROMCompanyLIMIT 2, 3;¶--or¶SELECT *FROMCompanyLIMIT 3OFFSET 2;¶¶¶¶Подзапросы.Видыподзапросов.¶¶Asubqueryisaqueryembeddedwithinanotherqueryandisenclosedinparentheses.Itisexecutedbeforethemainquery,exceptforcorrelatedsubqueries.Subqueriescanbeusedinthe `SELECT`, `FROM`, `WHERE`, `HAVING`, `INSERT`, `UPDATE`,and `DELETE`statements.¶¶Single-row,single-columnsubquery —returnsasinglevalue.Commonlyusedinconditionswith\'WHERE\'clause.¶ ...WHEREsalary > (SELECTAVG(salary)FROMEmployees);¶¶Multi-row,single-columnsubquery —returnsmultiplerowsandonecolumnanditrequiresspecialoperatorssuchasALL,INandANY:¶-ALLoperator —theconditionmustbetrueforallreturnedvalues:¶\r...WHERE 200 >ALL (SELECTpriceFROMRooms);¶-INoperator —checksifavalueexistsinthesetofreturnedvalues:¶\r...WHEREidIN (SELECTDISTINCTowner_idFROMRoomsWHEREprice >= 150)¶-ANYoperator —returnsTRUEifatleastonevalueexistsinthesetofreturnedvalues:¶\r...WHEREid =ANY (SELECTDISTINCTowner_idFROMRoomsWHEREprice >= 150)¶¶Multi-columnsubqueries —returnmultiplecolumnsandmultiplerows (derivedtables).Theyareusedtomatchvaluesinthemainquerywithvaluesinthesubquery.¶ ...WHERE (room_id,price)IN (SELECTid,priceFROMRooms);¶¶Correlatedsubqueries —refertooneormorecolumnsfromthemainqueryandareexecutedforeachrowofthemainquery,whichcannegativelyaffectperformancewithlargedatavolumes.', 1);
