(6, 1, 6, 1, 'Обобщённоетабличноевыражение,CTE,операторWITH,Union [ALL],INTERSECT,EXCEPT.ОсновныеразличиямеждуViewиCTE:¶¶ACommonTableExpression (CTE)isatemporarydatasetcreatedforthedurationofasinglequeryandnotstoredinthedatabase.Itisusedtosimplifycomplexqueriesandsupportrecursion.Itiscreatedusingthe `WITH ...AS (subquery)`syntax.¶¶WITHAeroflot_trips (aeroflot_plane,town_from,town_to)AS¶ (¶SELECTplane,town_from,town_toFROMCompany¶INNERJOINTripONTrip.company =Company.id¶WHEREname =\'Aeroflot\'¶)¶SELECT *FROMAeroflot_trips;¶¶-UNIONcombinestheresultsofmultiplequeriesortableswiththesamestructure,removingduplicates.Tokeepduplicatevalues,useUNIONALL.¶-INTERSECTreturnsrowsthatarepresentinbothqueries.¶-EXCEPTreturnsrowsfromthefirstquerythatarenotpresentinthesecond.¶¶##MaindifferencesbetweenViewandCTE:¶-AViewisstoredinthedatabase,whereasaCTEisatemporarythatexistsonlywithinasinglequery.¶-AViewdisplaysdata,whileaCTEcreatesatemporarysetforsubqueries.¶-AViewcanbeupdatedordeleted;aCTEcannot.¶-BothViewandCTEcanbeusedtosimplifycomplexqueriesandreusingthemainquery,howeveraCTEallowsyoutoperformiterationorrecursiveoperationswithinaquery.¶¶¶¶ОператорCASE,функцияIF,IFNULL,NULLIF¶¶3¶¶¶¶ОператорыINSERT,UPDATE,DELETEиTRUNCATE.¶¶**INSERTINTO** -usedtoaddnewrecordstoatable.Toinsertvalues,usethe `VALUES`clause,specifyingthedatainparenthesesseparatedbycommas.Theprimarykeymustbeunique,ifaduplicatevalueisinserted,anerrorwillbethrown.Forauto-generatingkeys,attributessuchas `AUTO_INCREMENT`inMySQLor `SERIAL`inPostgreSQLareused:¶Forinsertswithuniqueindexes,youcanuseacountofexistingrows:INSERTINTOGoodsSELECTCOUNT(*) + 1,поле1,полеNFROMGoods;¶ **UPDATE** -usedtoupdateexistingrecords.Thefieldstobechangedarespecifiedafterthe `SET`operator,andtheconditionisspecifiedinthe `WHERE`clause.Without `WHERE`,allrowsinthetablewillbeupdated:UPDATEимя_таблицыSETполе1 =значение1,полеN =значениеN [WHEREусловие];¶ **DELETE** -usedtodeleterecordsfromatable.If `WHERE`isnotspecified,allrecordswillbedeleted:DELETEFROMимя_таблицы [WHEREусловие];¶ **TRUNCATE** —unlike `DELETE`,itsimplydropsthetabledataandrecreatestheemptytableinternally.Thisworksfasterbecause `DELETE`removesrowsonebyone.SomeDBMSautomaticallyuse `TRUNCATE`whena `DELETE`querydoesnotcontain `WHERE`or `LIMIT`:TRUNCATETABLEtable_name;¶**TRUNCATE**hasseveraldifferences:¶-Triggersdonotfire,inparticular,thedeletetrigger.¶-Doesnotlogrowdeletionsinthetransactionlog.¶-Resetstheidentitycountertoitsinitialvalue.¶-Requirestablemodificationpermissions.¶**Deletingrecordsinmulti-tablequeries:**¶Ifa `DELETE`queryusesa `JOIN`,youmustspecifyfromwhichtablestherecordsshouldbedeleted.¶¶¶¶Операторыдлясозданияиудалениятаблицибазданных:CREATE,SHOWиDROP.IF [NOT]EXIST,USE,DESCRIBE,CASCADE¶¶2¶¶¶¶МасштабированиеSQLбазданных.Репликация,подходmaster-slave,Шардинг,ВертикальныйиГоризонтальныйшардинг.¶¶Databasescalingistheprocessofincreasingthecapacityandperformanceofadatabasetohandlelargerdatavolumesandmoreusers.Thecoreofdatascalingisdividingdataintogroupsanddistributingthemacrossseparateservers.Therearetwomainstrategies:replicationandsharding.¶¶Replicationitiswhenaduplicateofthedatabaseiscreated.Themostcommompatternisamaster-slave.Sincereadoperationsareusuallymuchmorefrequentthanwriteoperations,replicationallowsyoutooffloadthemainserverbymovingreadoperationstotheslave.Thedownsidesaredatadesynchronizationanddelaysincopyingfrommastertoslave.However,itisanexcellenttoolforensuringfaulttolerance.Replicationcanbecombinedwithsharding.¶¶-Master —themaindatabaseserverwhereallwritesandupdatesoccur.¶-Slave —asecondarydatabaseserverthatcopiesalldatafromthemaster.Datashouldbereadfromthisserver.Therecanbemultipleslaveservers.¶¶Shardingistheprocessofsplittingasingledatabaseintoseparatepartssothateachpartcanbehostedonadedicatedserver.Therearetwokindsofsharding:verticalandhorizontal.¶¶-Verticalshardingisthepracticeofmovingatableorgroupoftablestoaseparateserver.¶-Horizontalsharding —splittingasingletableacrossdifferentservers.Thisisnecessaryforverylargetablesthatcannotfitonasingleserver.¶¶¶¶ОсновыиндексоввSQLServer¶¶Indexesaredatastructuresthatspeedupqueryprocessing,likeatableofcontentsinabookhelpsyoufindthedesiredinformation.Forexample,whenanindexiscreatedonaprimarykeySQLServerwillfirstfindtheindexandthenusetheindextoquicklyfindtheentirerow.Withoutanindex,afulltablescanwouldbeperformed,whichcantakemuchlonger.However,indexescanslowdownwriteoperationslikeINSERT,UPDATE,DELETE,becauseindexmustbeupdatedtoo.Indexesarecreatedforcolumnsintablesandviews,exceptforcolumnswithlargedatatypessuchasTEXT,IMAGEorVARCHAR.Indexesaredividedintoclusteredandnon-clustered,andtherearealsoheaps.¶¶B-treeindex —isabalancedtree,buteachnodecontainspages,whosedataarelinkedinasortedlinkedlist,andeachlevelofthetreeisalsolinkedtoneighboringnodes,makingadoublylinkedlist.TheleavesoftheB-treecontaineithertheactualdataorpointerstothedata.Inthecaseofaclusteredindex,theleafnodescontaintheactualdatarows,whileinthecaseofanon-clusteredindex,theleafnodescontainkeysandpointerstotheactualdatarows.¶¶¶¶Кучи,КластеризованныйиНекластеризованныйиндекс.Составнойиндекс,Уникальныйиндекс,Покрывающийиндекс.¶¶Aheapsisatablewheredataisstroredwithoutanyspecificorderandindexes.Accessingandsearchingthroughsuchdataisperformedsequentiallybyscanningpages.Heapsaresuitableforstoringasmallamountsofdata.¶¶Aclusteredindex (B-treeindex)isanindexthatstoresdatabysortedkeyinitsnodes.Becauseofthis,youcanonlyhaveoneclusteredindexpertable.ThebestchoiceforakeyisusuallyanID,asitisalwaysuniqueandshort,andnewdataisaddedtotheend,sothereisnoneedtorebalancethetree,whichimprovesperformanceaslongastherootnode\'srangeisnotexceeded,andthenodeorleafdoesnotoverflow.¶¶Anon-clusteredindexisanindexwhosenodesstoreseitherpointerstothedatarowsinthetableortotheclusteredindexkeyifitexists.Youcancreatemultiplenon-clusteredindexesforasingletable.¶¶Acompositeindexisanindexbuiltonmultiplecolumns,upto 16columnsorupto 900bytesinsize.Itcanbeeitherclusteredornon-clustered.Dataisorderedfirstbythefirstcolumn,thenbythesecond,andsoon.¶¶Auniqueindexguaranteesthatallvaluesintheindexedcolumnorcombinationofcolumnsareunique.Itcanbeeitherclusteredornon-clustered.Auniqueindexisautomaticallycreatedfortheprimarykeyifitisnotclustered.¶¶Acoveringindexallowsaquerytoretrieveallthenecessarydatadirectlyfromtheindexleaveswithoutaccessingthetable\'srecords.Coveringindexesarefasterthanothersbuttakeupmorespace.Theycanbeeitherclusteredornon-clustered.¶¶B-treeindex —describedabove (balancedtreestructure).¶¶¶¶ОконнаяфункциявSQL (OVER)¶¶1¶¶¶¶ЧтотакоеORM?ВчемпреимуществаORM?ВчемнедостаткиORMикогдаеелучшенеиспользовать?¶¶AnORM (Object-RelationalMapper)isatechnologythatallowsyoutoworkwithdatabaseusing .NETobjects.Itcreatesalayerbetweendatabasesand .NETobjects,andautomaticallygeneratesSQLcodetocreatetablesbasedonclassesandviceversa.¶¶Advantages:ItfreesdevelopersfromwritingSQLqueries,andallcodegeneratedbytheORMiswell-testedandoptimized.WorkingthroughanORMmakesiteasiertoupdate,maintain,andreusetables,andmuchfunctionalityisavailable \"outofthebox,\"unlikewritingqueriesmanually.¶¶Themaindisadvantagesincludeapotentiallossofperformance,astheORMmaygeneratesuboptimalSQLqueries.ItisalsohardertotrackerrorsandtheactualSQLqueriescomparedtodirectprocedurecallsorhand-writtenqueries.ThereislittlepointinusinganORMiftherearenorelationshipsbetweentables,orifthedatabaseinterfaceisprimarilystoredprocedures.¶¶ExamplesEntityFramework /EntityFrameworkCoreorNHibernate. ---¶¶¶¶ВчемразницамеждуEagerloading,LazyLoadingвEFиexplicitloading?¶¶Eagerloadingmeansrelateddataisloadedtogetherwiththemaindatainasinglequery.Thisisimplementedusingthe `Include()`method,whichistranslatedintoaJOIN.Thishelpsavoidadditionalqueriestothedatabasewhenaccessingrelateddata.¶¶Explicitloadingistheprocessofloadingrelateddatausingthe `Load()`method.Afterloadingthedata,youcanaccessitagainthroughthe `Local`property (db.Users.Local)itrepresentsthecollectionloadedintomemoryusingthe `Load()`or `ToList()`methods.Thankstothis,EFdoesnotexecuteadditionalqueriestothedatabase,butworkswiththeloadeddata.¶¶Lazyloadingistheautomaticloadingofrelateddatawhenyouaccessit.However,itmaysendmultiplequeriestoretrievejustonerecord,ormanyqueriesifthenavigationpropertyisacollection,soitshouldbeusedcarefullyandyoushouldcheckthequeriesbeingsent.Touseit,youneedtoaddtheproxyNuGetpackage `MS.EFC.Proxies`,configurethedatacontextbycalling `UseLazyLoadingProxies()`,andmarkallnavigationpropertiesasvirtual.Theclassesthemselvesmustbeopenforinheritance.¶¶¶¶КакиекомпонентыархитектурыEntityFrameworkвызнаете?¶¶EntityFrameworkisanobject-relationalmapper¹ (O/RM)thatallowsyoutoworkwithadatabaseusing .NETobjects.ItcanalsoautomaticallygenerateSQLcodetocreatetablesbasedonclassesandviceversa.EFfitsbetweentheDataLayerandthedatabase.¶¶TheArchitectureoftheEFincludesseveralcomponents:¶ -TheEntityDataModel(EDM) -abstractsthelogicalorrelationalschemaandusesathree-layeredapproach:¶ -TheConceptualModel (C)containsthemodelclassesandtheirrelationships.¶ -TheMappingmodel (C-S)includesinformationabouthowtheconceptualmodelismappedtothestoragemodel.¶ -TheStoragemodel (S)representstheschemaoftheunderlying¹database,whichincludestables,views,Keys,storedprocedures,andtheirrelationships.¶¶ -LINQtoEntities -isaquerylanguageusedtowritequeriesagainsttheobjectmodel.Itreturnsentities,thataredefinedintheconceptualmodel.¶-EntitySQL -isanotherquerylanguagejustlikeLINQtoEntities,however,itisalittlemoredifficult.¶¶-TheObjectServicesLayer -istheContext;¶¶-EntityClientDataProvider -isresponsibleforconvertingLINQ-to-EntitiesorEntitySQLqueriesintoaSQLquerythatunderlyingdatabaseunderstands.ItcommunicateswiththeADO .Netdataprovider²whichsendsorretrieves³datafromthedatabase.¶ -ADO .NETDataProviderlayercommunicateswiththedatabaseusingstandardADO.Net.¶¶¶¶EntityFrameworkContextClass.WhatisanEntityintheEntityFramework?Typesofnavigationproperties.¶¶DbContext -itisabridgebetweenyourentitiesandtheunderlyingdatabasewhichrepresentsthesession¹ofinteractionbetweentheapplicationsandthedatasource.AninstanceofDbContextcombinestheUn